{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality","id":633531,"title":"Reasserting reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-20T10:02:27-07:00","id":633531,"title":"Reasserting reality","content":"If a mage does something stupidly silly: 10 dragons, flying Ford T, kick of a thousand aggravated, 20 laserswords. Giant robots etc<br /> <br /> What do you guys do to reassert reality? <br /> <br /> Myself: I assume the domino effect is there and that ihe spell now a beacon for paradox spirits. If it's a major event, third parties will start to be interested oreven intervene.<br /> <br /> What would you do? What to do with a lasting vulgar effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","user":"AgentCunningham","date":"myself included) 08-20-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T10:31:58-07:00","id":633573,"title":"","content":"Aside of some of those ideas just being Evil-ST-fodder if not blocked by a resounding 'No!', I would pretty much do as Phil suggests in the books: Make the punishment fit the crime.<br /> <br /> Have the dragons suddenly become uncontrolled and go berzerk. as reality begins to kill them, their rampage destroying everything the mage holds dear. Before dieing into a goop.<br /> <br /> Have the kick of a thousand aggravated (Those calculations were just plain silly in that thread) shatter the Mage. Completely. Welcome to reality suddenly deciding to enforce physics after all and the fact that every kinetic force causes an equal counterforce being the last thing the Mage experiences, period.<br /> <br /> Giant robots? Technocratic near-Code-Ragnarok. Kiss the character goodbye. No reality adjustment needed to handle that in modern times. NWO will make sure Media Control prepares the appropriate mind Procedures and channels.<br /> <br /> ...a flying Ford T actually almost falls under a tame technomage-tinkering case. I can see that happening. And the thing failing if spotted over a larger settlement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-20-2015, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T10:53:41-07:00","id":633585,"title":"","content":"Most of these things seldom become an issue, because the PCs rarely amass the personal power needed to field armies of dragons. In such a case it would allways be the question how you would handle dragons under normal circumstances. I would make them massive Thaumivores, requiring them to consume vast amounts of Quintessence to stay in concensual reality, in whatever form is appropriate to the specific dragon (lava, virgins, gold, etc.). They would also fizzle rather fast once they confronted large groups of humans. So burning down villages may work, but attacking Manhatten on the back of your awesome dragon may be a bit of a bad idea. This would probably show in the form of the dragon sicken and dying quickly in an allergic reaction to some big city toxin.<br /> <br /> Building a flying car or a lightsaber is vulgar and will incur the associated cost in paradox each time it's used. It'd again only fail with a large audience.<br /> <br /> As for something vulgar that is lasting (say your mage would like to turn every bullet shot at him into a flower and does a long ritual with many successes to accomplish this for a long time) : I would personally assert paradox each scene the affect becomes active (thus none at creation, since the field itself is invisible and coincidental as long as it's not active, though the mage would have to roll for vulgar with witness difficulty if he wanted the shield to be active in front of witnesses - even if he was in a sanctum). For effects that are blatantly vulgar the effect itself may be eroded aswell if witnesses. So a mage causing his skin to emit a strong light for the next year would (besides getting ridiculous amounts of paradox outside the umbra/sanctum) find his spell fading if he stayed around sleepers. If he managed to hold of paradox somehow from taking care of it with backlashes. Again it kinda depends on the amount of sleepers witnessing here.<br /> <br /> Alternativly it wouldn't be too far fetched to assign an amount of permadox for vulgar effects with long durations, especially those that are consistently on and thus vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T12:09:33-07:00","id":633644,"title":"","content":"Aw. I actually posted my response on the other thread (I fail at forums, sorry). I hope you don't mind me putting it here:<br /> <br /> --<br /> [It] depends on the type of effect. If the effect is perpetual, than the rule that I'd use is the one for permanent pattern alterations like gills, certain cybernetic enhancements, or raising an attribute over 5: namely the mage would have a point (or more depending on the properties of the effect) of permanent paradox which would not be burned until the effect stops. I like this rule because it is something manageable, but it still encourages the mage to be cautious and avoid too much additional vulgar magic (as backlash, when not all the paradox can actually get burned off, can get pretty nasty.)<br /> <br /> If the effect must be activated to be used: like a wand of fireballs, then I would apply the same temporary paradox that I would if the mage was fast casting that same effect every time he uses it.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:19:10-07:00","id":633737,"title":"","content":"We already have the pattern bleeding for,life effects. And casted effectsgenerate paradox at each activation.<br /> <br /> The wand of fireball is an activvation item and has paradox each time it will cast, or not if it's a lighter! A 24/7 featherfall ring would not have an activation phase. Degraded over time for matter effects when you can select the duration seems inelegant...<br /> <br /> The problem arrives more for standby spells, continual spells and making the spirits do the dirty work fOr you.<br /> <br /> Maybe pattern spiders or paradox spirits that will flock to the area? Every vulgar continuous effects counts for paradox backlash paradox spirit p 522 And for domino effects as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T13:41:47-07:00","id":633753,"title":"","content":"You want to keep Paradox spirits up your sleeves for people who accumulated alot of paradox, I think. They should not be something common, more something that really makes your players (and NPCs) shit their pants. They are quite literally sentinent paradox coming to bust your ass. Pattern Spiders I wouldn't involve since well, it's not Werewolf, the pattern Spiders in 99,99% of the cases can't or won't do anything to you as long as you are in concensual reality.<br /> <br /> A 24/7 featherfall ring activates every time it slows your fall, basically. Sure it's active the rest of the time too, but in the instances where the effect actually works beyond the believable it becomes vulgar and thus attracts paradox.<br /> <br /> Making effects permanent with Matter is really easy, but that's beside the point. You can built an impenetrable armor with Matter 5, Duration doesn't really matter, but let's assume it's a month. Now you go and fight a whole army of cops in the streets of NY. Sure you can tank bullets in skirmishes quite easily (though you may attract some paradox doing so). But as soon as the press helicopter is hovering over you while the police calls in the national guard to deal with this &quot;unstoppable juggernaut&quot; your armor suddenly starts showing dents and finally is penetrated by a bullet. Of course realistically you have at that point long been stopped by a technocratic sniper using &quot;armor piercing bullets&quot;, nerve gas or whatever, but that is beside the point.<br /> <br /> Domino effect should be for incresingly unbelievable coincidences, imo. If anything doing a lot of vulgar spells should make your magic easier in a place/time/company, since people are seeing your spells and after a moment of disblief probably begin to accept that what you are doing has to be possible somehow, afterall they are seeing it.<br /> <br /> Spirit magic actually is coincidental a lot of the times, at least if it is actually the spirit employing his charms. As long as you don't help him doing so directly of course (by carrying it across the gauntlet with Spirit 4 for example) you are fine. Think of it like using MInd to sic a horde of Sorcerors on your enemies. You are not doing anything impossible, they are, using static magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:34:12-07:00","id":633802,"title":"","content":"Don't forget paradox flaws. Those can be fun for the small niggling cases where a paradox spirit is a waste. And you can scale them: small inconvenient ones for small offenses (slit pupiled eyes for a regular shapeshifter are noticeable, but manageable if you don't mind wearing sunglasses indoors) to something a bit worse (Oh, dear. The Son of Ether's regular vulgar force use has led to him having a faint magnetic charge...he might want to stay out of computer labs), to something pretty insane, (Yes, your philosopher's stone is very impressive, Mr. Solificati, but now everything you touch turns to gold. That's going to be one hell of an effective diet plan.) -- ideally these should be temporary of course. There are far better ways to actually kill off characters. :-P<br /> <br /> Spirits really should be a big deal, I like to remember that &quot;Father's Day&quot; episode from the new Doctor Who, when I think of how scary Paradox manifestations should be. They definitely should be used sparingly, so they don't lose impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 08-20-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T17:42:08-07:00","id":634046,"title":"","content":"I am completely against saying &quot;No!&quot; to a player, unless the player really wants to do something that the character can't. Instead, just make him face the consequences. Want to create dragons? Ok, 1 paradox generated for each dragon and now you got giant flying monsters flying around trying to kill him. And this will call technocrats attention.<br /> <br /> For long duration effects, every scene it goes on is a good call, but not really fair, because the mage had to make a lot of successes just to make the effect last. Treating it as if the mage casted again is throwing those successes away.<br /> Maybe just generate paradox when the effect is casted, like the rules says. What's the worst that could happen? For big and lasting effects there is patter bleeding and permadox anyway...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T21:08:54-07:00","id":634230,"title":"","content":"The problem it's that those actions destroy the setting.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if the national guard ends stopping you, the point it's that Mage it's a game where the protagonist need to subtly adjust Reality in order to use his powers freely. That's why there's an Ascension War for the minds of the masses in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you can just release 10 dragons for 10 (Or 1 paradox point, or none, dependant on what rule-hole you found to hide yourself), there's no way that humanity wouldn't notice.<br /> <br /> There's no enough &quot;lulz, that's fake&quot; comments in the world to silence 10 dragons eating people and burning buildings in the Center of New York, in daylight. This it's going to cause a mayhem, and there's no enough pattern bleeding around to stop it in time.<br /> <br /> People speaks, people listens to other people that they consider friends and family, and the news of this sort of thing would run free no mater what kind of means you use to silence it, blowing a major hole in &quot;the Masquerade&quot;. If any mage can do so any day without immediate reprisals, then the setting blows up.<br /> <br /> This it's not about silencing your players, this it's about not letting that a <i>bad designed rule(s)</i> interferes with the mood of the game that your players intended to play. Again, think on things like &quot;Czar Vargo&quot; case. It's obvious that, when you look at these cases, when you look on how the setting it's described, than mages loosing dragons upon the world can't happen for more reasons that merely the mage's common sense. <hr /><br /> But yea, those are the rules. I can't discuss that. So you've found the classic ways of powergaming in Mage (the classic<i> ritual abuse</i>, and several &quot;holes&quot; to avoid Paradox,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/631573-life-rituals\">as per this thread</a>), and proved than M20 it's more prone to powergaming, and more unbalanced, than previous editions.<br /> <br /> Saying that &quot;rules are rules&quot; solves nothing. Sure, those are the rules. They're poorly designed rules, that had various fixes (some of which where presented in the other thread) that didn't get into M20 (which doesn't always mean that they're not canon). The fact that they didn't get into M20 does nothing to undermine the roleplaying value of those rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-21-2015, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T00:39:34-07:00","id":634336,"title":"","content":"<b>Aleph</b>, You should first remember that this game IS about insurmountable power. With preparation a Mage can do anything. And yes, this includes blowing up in the face of the Consensus regularly.<br /> <br /> The game is about delivering consequences for your decisions, but never about stopping you from taking such decisions. If a player really can and want to attack Manhattan with a giant five-headed multicolored dragon and a plain-face villain mounted in a nightmare, that is exactly what the player will get.<br /> <br /> It isn't just the rules. It IS the spirit of the setting. Suspension of Disbelief applies here, don't think too much why the setting didn't blew up yet. It is because of internal logic, not real life logic.<br /> <br /> People at the World of Darkness aren't like normal people. They are more apathetic. They are less informed (and real life people aren't all that clever, either). And on top of that, in Ascension's case, they are regular target of magic(k). The Technocratic Union works with the same level of power to control damage, and they're not the only ones. One of the perfectly viable plot hooks of the Tradition's PCs is the mad Mage trying to do completely unreasonable shit. Like conjuring Tiamat and the Venger. And that's a problem precisely because it WILL work.<br /> <br /> With that said, I would stick to normal Paradox rules first for the casting. IF the casting didn't accrued Paradox (maybe a Sanctum), then normal Paradox could accrue when the magic is activated.<br /> <br /> But if the effect was continuous and without Paradox at the casting, I would just give Permadox. It is the most sensible response in my opinion. Being harsher than that in Paradox, like every scene, is tantamount to prohibiting the effect, what isn't fair in my book, but can already make a hard time for the Mage on the near future.<br /> <br /> For the use of Spirit magic, I would use spirits in general. The same way that Mind magic have consequences if you abuse, the Umbra have landscapes and denizens. Those critters are hardly an issue on most occasions, but frequent abuse can attract attention from the ones that CAN be an issue. They don't need to be Paradox spirits.<br /> <br /> You can also pervert the effects, attract strange attention, or send magic and magician together to other Realms, even Paradox ones. I find this better than just unraveling magic, I usually avoid to unravel it at first.<br /> <br /> So, in the end of the day, the dragon-rider will end up in a Paradox Realm full of bigger, nastier dragons, while the Union control damage making most people forget the incident or covering it with hyper-technology and clever use of Mind, Space and Time, and a cabal of Traditionalists just finish Venger in an alley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T03:10:46-07:00","id":634420,"title":"","content":"The setting it's created by the stuff that happens in it. That's why I mentioned Czar Vargos case, because it's implied in the Guide to the Traditions that if the Technocracy had the amount of power needed to make everyone in the world forget about that incident, then the Ascension War won't have lasted a day. As such, a massive Paradox Backlash seems more likely.<br /> Paradoxes that transcend the normal limitations are all over the plot, like when Syndicate crashed the market by doing a subtle, but massive, change to economy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that said, I would stick to normal Paradox rules first for the casting. IF the casting didn't accrued Paradox (maybe a Sanctum), then normal Paradox could accrue when the magic is activated.<br /> <br /> But if the effect was continuous and without Paradox at the casting, I would just give Permadox. It is the most sensible response in my opinion. Being harsher than that in Paradox, like every scene, is tantamount to prohibiting the effect, what isn't fair in my book, but can already make a hard time for the Mage on the near future.<br /> <br /> For the use of Spirit magic, I would use spirits in general. The same way that Mind magic have consequences if you abuse, the Umbra have landscapes and denizens. Those critters are hardly an issue on most occasions, but frequent abuse can attract attention from the ones that CAN be an issue. They don't need to be Paradox spirits.<br /> <br /> You can also pervert the effects, attract strange attention, or send magic and magician together to other Realms, even Paradox ones. I find this better than just unraveling magic, I usually avoid to unravel it at first. </div> </div> </div>The whole point of my post its that, because of several &quot;holes&quot; in the rules, all of these things won't happen (or would be irrelevant). Even giving Paradox when the magic it's &quot;activated&quot; seems to be outside of the rules for our OP. So no, no Paradox realm (nor a single Paradox point) for the lucky dragon summoner that knows so well the rules of Mage. That's the point.<br /> Is that the setting you saw when you readed the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-21-2015, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T03:54:36-07:00","id":634433,"title":"","content":"Aleph, when you have a spell that has no activation anymore, locked jn etc. you can't go around giving paradox, it's unfair. The caster did the extra success, difficulties for lenght, for the success etc.<br /> <br /> If home rules are applied one way, you get pc that will do alternative ways to profit from it, it's human nature. ex: spirit doing the heavy lifting and you dodge that paradox.<br /> <br /> When i read the book, and the game world, i saw a cold war between two mage group, vast supernatural forces vying for dwindling ressources (caerns, nodes), conspiracy on a large scale (technocracy, vampires,pentex), archmasters being there (bullying or being absent to force us to become adults with revised), reality changing with concensus, evil beyond imagination plotting to destroy the world (nephandi, doomsday cult, wyrm, sabbat), supernatural ecosystem, regulatory mechanism (weaver, pattern spirits, paradox spirits,werewolves, technocracy, the government, the media), veils and traditions to hide the truth... It's a completely complex world that is there to &quot;get you&quot; if you are a bit too vulgar... <br /> <br /> The lucky dragon mage has enough on his plate after casting that supremely stupid 10 dragons. He skirted the rule, played within the parameters, risked a botch, did a crazy long ritual. The live dragons will have pattern bleeding, if it's a spirit dragon, they will need to be fed or they will have a limited timespan/atitude. there are enough rules within that world to punish players that are pushing it with vulgarity. That caster must have had a good reason if not he's going to get a council punishment ( branding, gilgul, brainwipe, sweeping floors, banishment to an horizon realm etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T04:28:13-07:00","id":634445,"title":"","content":"Again, punishing the mage it's not te point, the point it's that if I can summon 10 dragons in the center of the greatest capitals of the world, they're going to kill hundreds or thousands of people, and destroy whole city blocks before pattern bleeding steps in. The police and the military will get involved. There's a limit to suspension of disbelief regardings on how stupid and apathetic can WoD people be, before turning too far away from our world. Some things just don't vanish. If they did, then breaking the Masquerade with a display of Celerity 5 would be a non issue (hardly deserving of a strong punishment).<br /> <br /> The only way to cope with such a thing happening it's, either making Paradox clean the mess, or overpowering the Technocracy, to the point that they can really clean such disasters (and then justify why they can't just make religions go down the toilet the same way, and win the war).<br /> <br /> The fact that WoD it's predatory, and weird, don't demonstrate that such things as dragons killing hundreds of people DO happen every year or so. These are the sort of things that happen in Gehena, and similar events...<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Oh, and for the record. &quot;an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick (given new limbs or other characteristics that are not part of the creature\u2019s original Pattern) suffers Pattern bleeding&quot;<br /> <br /> A summoned dragon isn't &quot;an organism that has been radically altered by Life magick &quot;, but a created organism/pattern. The pattern of the dragon it's &quot;original&quot;. You didn't buffed a lizard, merely created a whole new dragon. Thus, it can be argued than it wouldn't suffer from pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> Unbelief should kick in, as per Paradox rules for created beings. But, oh, it's effects aren't clearly delineated, so it's not a rule. Or is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-21-2015, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T05:56:14-07:00","id":634483,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember is that by the standards of many other game settings cWOD is overpowered with it's supernatural abilities. The rules are fairly loose so that the ST (and players) can have ample freedom to develop their stories. This does not mean the rules/setting are bad or poorly designed only that responsibility on the ST/players part must be taken to not &quot;break&quot; the desired setting for the story. <br /> <br /> This is the reason I personally never recommend WW games to younger beginning players. <br /> <br /> At some point we have all power gamed. Doing so in the cWOD makes a mess real fast due to the most limiting aspect of curtailing what can or can't be done is the setting, not hard rules. If player's, and even ST's, want to abuse the system its not very hard to do, and if thats the style of game that is wanted there is nothing wrong with that. If however that is not the type of story being told and a player(s) wants to &quot;rules lawyer&quot; their way to outlandish circumstances expext the ST to &quot;Golden Rule&quot; the consequences. <br /> <br /> I realize that many times people consider a game that needs house rules or the Golden Rule of GMing to work must be broken or is being ran by an incompetent GM. It should be remembered though that the game rules aren't written by lawyers. If they were then most loopholes and contradictions wouldn't be there to be exploited. The book would probably be 3 times as big though and we would all need law degrees to understand it. <br /> <br /> I guess my point, if i still have one, is that its pretty easy to find ways in Mage to do some ridiculous things. There are also plenty of ways to resrict them though not always by hard, fast rules. If your player constantly feels the need to challenge these things then maybe Mage isn't the game for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 08-21-2015, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T06:07:40-07:00","id":634509,"title":"","content":"I think you should handle the situation in game instead of House rule to prohibit the mage to do what he wants in a game where everything is possible. And remember that to create 10 dragons for a long period of time would require a LOT of successes and high spheres.<br /> Ruling like you say solves nothing. The mage could simply fly to the top of a building and cast a giant energy ball throwing in the midle of the city.<br /> The fireballs wouldn't suffer unbelief,neither permadox or pattern bleeding, because they are instantaneous. <br /> You would handle it in game with consequences thag aren't good for the mage. When the player stops having fun because of them you could talk to him off game and ask why the hell he is trying to fuck with the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T06:15:43-07:00","id":634517,"title":"","content":"Aleph, it's a created vulgar being, it's worst than putting gills on a cat. Of course it's gonna patterrn bleed. Created from nothings counts as a &quot;radical life pattern alterating&quot; in my book!<br /> <br /> You can't punish the mage for doing his stunt as he has casted it following the casting rules AND it was a mighty feat, you can't give paradox after the cast. It's unfair. <br /> <br /> It's a slippery slope. It leads to cheats like using spirits to do the &quot;heavy lifting&quot;, ie summon a spirit, mold him, brainwash him, cajole him and then let him do the effects without your assistance and other methods. <br /> <br /> I have mentioned quite a few times in this forum that i am all for consequences. I thought iwasclear on that. I'm against creating rules to limit and punish a successful casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T06:34:11-07:00","id":634531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunningham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=634433#post634433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aleph, when you have a spell that has no activation anymore, locked jn etc. you can't go around giving paradox, it's unfair. The caster did the extra success, difficulties for lenght, for the success etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's not entirely true. Or at least it hasn't always been. Some time ago, in an example of how Revised Paradox rules worked, Malcolm Sheppard gave an example of a fellow who was using a stealth/invisibility spell (via manipulating shadows) to climb down a wall. At the top, it was fine, there were shadows and it was dark. As he descended, search lights and such eventually grew too bright and the spell would have to be dropped unless the player went full on vulgar. He did, and took the paradox. (The exact post is here: <a href=\"http://shadownessence.se/forum/topic/15886-how-paradox-works/?page=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://shadownessence.se/forum/topic...-works/?page=1</a> It's still a helpful read, I think, even though Revised rules are no longer the default.)<br /> <br /> Now this version wasn't a published rule (closest comparison would be creator-written informal errata) and I honestly can't remember if a similar example made it into an actual sourcebook. This was also Revised Paradox, which does work differently from Mage 20, though whether it would in this particular area is unclear (I'm hoping the Sphere Guide will address it). But it does at least provide a sample situation for when environmental factors can change whether or not a spell is vulgar or coincidental while it has already been cast.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, something like 10 dragons already starts off so vulgar that I can't really imagine a situation where I feel it would be appropriate to add more paradox on top of it. But there is at least anecdotal precedent to justify the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  For accuracy 08-21-2015, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T06:55:39-07:00","id":634563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunningham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=634517#post634517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aleph, it's a created vulgar being, it's worst than putting gills on a cat. Of course it's gonna patterrn bleed. Created from nothings counts as a &quot;radical life pattern alterating&quot; in my book!<br /> <br /> You can't punish the mage for doing his stunt as he has casted it following the casting rules AND it was a mighty feat, you can't give paradox after the cast. It's unfair.<br /> <br /> It's a slippery slope. It leads to cheats like using spirits to do the &quot;heavy lifting&quot;, ie summon a spirit, mold him, brainwash him, cajole him and then let him do the effects without your assistance and other methods.<br /> <br /> I have mentioned quite a few times in this forum that i am all for consequences. I thought iwasclear on that. I'm against creating rules to limit and punish a successful casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aleph's got a point. Generation is not the same as alteration. Alteration means that there is a pre-existing &quot;correct&quot; pattern from which you are deviating, generation creates a pattern whole and complete. Since there is no deviation from a pre-existing pattern, one could argue that the strain that would cause pattern bleeding would not be in effect. (Pattern bleeding would be caused, in this interpretation, by the strain of energy and matter trying to &quot;correct itself&quot; to the original pattern.) You would of course still have to fuel the dragon-construct with the appropriate Quintessence to keep it able to exist at all, which would be its own difficulty, in my opinion. Dragons undoubtedly have very large appetites, so to speak.<br /> <br /> It's an interesting thought. I'm not sure how I'd rule on it in one of my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 08-21-2015, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:00:19-07:00","id":634567,"title":"","content":"A giant energy ball always generate normal Paradox, which means that I don't have to houserule anything in this case. In this case the rules work as intended (it's a Vulgar display).<br /> But that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> As I said, the problem it's not the mage, but to keep those &quot;in game situations&quot; that you speak about from destroying the setting.<br /> I don't care if the mage get's punished or escapes and lives happily thereafter.Of course such actions will demand reprimand from in game factions. What I do care it's that such actions may call for an unrealistic response or blow the setting.<br /> <br /> Either humanity discover that magic it's real, or an Archmage steps in and reverses time, or Technocracy brainwashes everyone. As Tuch says, there're plenty of ways of wrecking the game, and plenty of ways of impeding these.<br /> <br /> Would you be happy if instead of &quot;house ruling&quot; I sended insanely powerfull Time 2 mages to foil your casting, because they predicted the consecuences? That's the least world shattering answer that occurs to me. However, that also impedes your casting...<br /> <br /> But, even then, why don't houserule? Paradox it's here to punish the hubris of mages, and to protect reality.<br /> If it can't do so because of a hole in the rules that allows for vulgar displays without Paradox, and you can fix that hole and have a more robust and coherent setting as consequence, I see no reason to not doing so. Even if it doesn't stops the mage from doing and succeding in it's crazy ritual, Paradox shouldn't be inconsequential, it's one of the most important aspects of the setting, one of the principal reasons for the entire Asencion War.<br /> <br /> Besides, many of those that you call &quot;house rules&quot;, are actual rules of the system. The rule that cancels a vulgar spell when you get it out of the Sanctum it's canon for revised. Unbelief existed from the very begining, and it was stated to be the Paradox that forced dragons and other magical beings and creations to leave the earth. I'm not inventing these, merely applying them regardless if they're in M20 or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-21-2015, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:24:05-07:00","id":634577,"title":"","content":"I think a new creations and pattern bleeding would depend on what the creature is and how it is introduced to reality. A dragon I can't really see anyone buying so it would suffer badly. Bigfoot on the other hand has all kinds of believers (my brother-in-law included). If set up to be discovered in North America or Canada by a team of scientists(?) searching for such a creature I would say the pattern bleeding, though still present, would be 1 or 2 points a day. There are enough people who want to believe in such a thing that even though there are skeptics it would be hard to argue with the real thing standing in front of you. Even a lost dinosaur such as Loch Ness Monster would have an easier time existing.<br /> <br /> A dragon on the otherhand would suffer from huge disbelief. The resulting paradox (manifested as pattern bleeding) will destroy it quickly. I cant remember if its the Bygon Bestiary or another supplement that mentions that such fantastic creature survive no more than a few hours in the modern world.<br /> <br /> Now relasing such a creature wouldn't inflict paradox on the Mage after the effect has completed, it would only effect the creature with pattern bleeding and possibly paradox spirits or realms coming into existence as well depending on the circumstances.<br /> <br /> If however the Mage were to alter himself, say by transforming his own pattern to that of a dragon, then additional paradox and, or permadox would be incurred upon entering the consensus as the effect has now become vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:28:23-07:00","id":634580,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that while I don't have any objection to a storyteller embracing a player's very crazy idea and running with it, I think there's always something that needs to be considered. What about the other players in your game? Are THEY willing to deal with the consequences of this one guy's crazy actions? Will they still have fun when the dragons are consuming everything in sight or when the Technocracy goes full brunt against them? (Heck, even in a one-on-one game, the storyteller counts as a player, would YOU have fun running this game?)<br /> <br /> As a storyteller, you really have the responsibility to try to be sure all the players are enjoying themselves and not to allow one person to ruin everyone else's fun. So if you allow something like the grand summoning of 12 golden dragons, then you really need to make sure your other players are on board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:58:10-07:00","id":634598,"title":"","content":"As i said, I would carry on in game, if this leads to a point where there is no more fun to any of the players, it should be discussed off game.<br /> Doing things like this is an obvious atempt to fuck with the game.<br /> Now, I don't agrre with house rules because there can be another player trying to do something way tinier that will be affected by this rule.<br /> The str is one example. The guy spends a lit of time and successes to buff his str and everytime he uses his str to do something he will still get a paradox point? Not fair.<br /> Same with the bulletproof silk shirt. M20 even have a similar hoodie and it doesn't generate paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:54:11-07:00","id":634638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=634420#post634420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I mentioned Czar Vargos case, because it's implied in the Guide to the Traditions that if the Technocracy had the amount of power needed to make everyone in the world forget about that incident, then the Ascension War won't have lasted a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you mean: 'The Week of Nightmares where the Technocracy managed to cover up and brainwash away multiple nukes and nightmarish creatures wracking the landscape of one of Earth's most densly populated areas'?<br /> <br /> *ducks*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T08:56:20-07:00","id":634639,"title":"","content":"The summoner of dragons has made a ritual and has probably been sitting on a corner mumbling for 4-5 game sessions to cast his spell. It can be a great project that is waiting for a biig roleplay payoff... the mad scientist making his giant robot for years in his basement and then the Big evil is showing up etc.<br /> <br /> At one point, the other players will create characters to take advantage of magick that is not penalized, foregoing sanctums to use cults, using spirits to create effects, create more artifacts to cast for you etc.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day: You cast a spell, get the success needed to do the effect, get the success for the duration you want and add all the modifiers. If it's vulgar you get a paradox, if not it's coincidental. <br /> <br /> You modify this and you will get players trying to dodge your home rules.<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of using the world and npc interaction to helppolice/curb the excess. We have a number of tools to do so.we so not need to invent them (i like flinty idea from the beginning of the thread personally though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","user":"AgentCunningham","date":".  Praise to flinty 08-21-2015, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:01:27-07:00","id":634642,"title":"","content":"(This is directed toward Darth Revan's post above. I apologize - I hadn't seen AgentCunningham's or Ambrosia's posts or I would have included a quotation for clarity)<br /> <br /> That depends on how he buffs his strength, if he does it over 5, Mage 20 (see Quantumboost's post on the life rituals thread) seems to indicate that he'd keep some permanent paradox until the effect ceases. (Then it can be burned like a normal paradox point.) That's not really a terrible consequence. (You wouldn't accumulate more temp paradox on top, unless he does some additional working.) I admit, I've never used the possible Genetic Flaw alternative, so I'm not sure how that would work in game.<br /> <br /> 651 of Mage 20 addresses Wonders and Paradox. It points out that a wonder gaining paradox is dependent on the coincidence/vulgar determination and the presence of witnesses at the time of its use. (I would read that qualification to mean that whether or not something is coincidental/vulgar could also be influenced by the context.). So if someone shoots from a distance and it's plausible that they missed, the silk shirt and hoodie would be fine and coincidental. If it's an unmistakable point blank shot in front of witnesses, I think you'd be getting paradox. It does appear clear from that section that the determination is made each time the wonder is used. I hope when the more involved Wonder rules that the book promises come out, we'll get a bit more detail about how to use this.<br /> <br /> The funny thing about an armored silk shirt is that you're less likely to get paradox if someone is shooting at you than if they tried to stab you or hit you with a bat. It's more plausible that someone could miss shooting, less so that a silk shirt would offer any sort of padding or insulation from a knife or blunt force. (...you might be able to argue that the blunt force could be mitigated by the attacker not hitting as hard as it looked, actually. The knife wound is trickier.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  Repeated attempts at clarity, sorry. 08-21-2015, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:02:42-07:00","id":634659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=634638#post634638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you mean: 'The Week of Nightmares where the Technocracy managed to cover up and brainwash away multiple nukes and nightmarish creatures wracking the landscape of one of Earth's most densly populated areas'?<br /> <br /> *ducks*</div> </div> </div> </div>+ 1 to ambrosia!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:34:50-07:00","id":634713,"title":"","content":"Ok let's not include wonders into this.<br /> You are using the rules right on the str example, but that's not what was proposed with house rules. House ruled, would generate paradox everytime the mage lifts a car (even with str 5).<br /> Instead of the silk wonder, think of a force field. It's extremely unfair to gain paradox every scene where there is a gunfight or knife stab when the mage have spent successss on duration and made a ritual.<br /> Paradox is gained only when the effect is cast, as a way of reality trying to balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:48:19-07:00","id":634727,"title":"","content":"Honestly, no. Reality is always a factor, not just at spell creation. I think that's been proven over and over again in these threads When the situation changes, paradox can become a factor again.<br /> <br /> This is how I usually do it: If the forcefield was cast as a vulgar effect without witnesses, I would probably allow the scene to play out without more. Unless witnesses show up. If that happens, the player gets to choose: &quot;drop the effect, or you get the witness paradox.&quot;<br /> <br /> If the forcefield was originally coincidental, then it would be situation dependent for me. One guy shooting from a distance is ok. If it's a point blank range shot where it is not remotely plausible that the bullet didn't hit, player gets the same warning : &quot;the coincidence is stretched too thin, so either drop the effect or go vulgar.&quot;<br /> <br /> I generally find this to be a reasonably fair approach. YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  Autocorrect hates me 08-21-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:51:20-07:00","id":634729,"title":"","content":"M20 don't differentiate with witness and without. It's just 1 paradox unless botch. The forcefield would get the 1 on creation and never more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:05:32-07:00","id":634771,"title":"","content":"I did misremember the rule (old rules stick in the head sometimes), but I'll stand by the rest. Under certain circumstances, there would be another paradox calculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:59:50-07:00","id":634858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=634729#post634729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 don't differentiate with witness and without. It's just 1 paradox unless botch. The forcefield would get the 1 on creation and never more.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it goes to a new scene due to duration I'd apply it again if the force field activated. Just like using a magic device would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T12:46:02-07:00","id":634954,"title":"","content":"That doesn't seems fair at all. This way would be better to use Life and get to soak aggravayed damage for 1 permadox. If the mage uses the forcefield in 3 conssecutive scenes, he will gather 3 (or much more if revised) paradox, which are much more dangerous than 1 permadox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:53:04-07:00","id":635044,"title":"","content":"Why is it unfair for one sphere to be more practical for certain purposes than others? They're not the same, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:14:35-07:00","id":635062,"title":"","content":"The life effect is giving permadox and pattern bleeding. I personaly find that way worse than 1 point of paradox per scence I use a forcefield. I can burn paradox. The permadox and pattern bleeding stays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":".  Spelling 08-21-2015, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T17:00:25-07:00","id":635156,"title":"","content":"Pattern bleeding can be healed with 1 success per day using Life 2. It's insignificant.<br /> I don't think that spheres differences are unfair, it's the house rule that is. Getting paradox for each scene that each buff a mage uses in combat is too much. Mages needs stuff like soaking pools and damage/attack bonus to survive. And the majority of them will let him do things that are pretty incredible for a sleeper to believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T17:11:42-07:00","id":635183,"title":"","content":"These &quot;house rules&quot; have never been a problem in the games I've ran over the last three years. And my players have never complained. <br /> <br /> Do your games have trouble with these things?<br /> <br /> Oh 1 more thing. Though it may not be the rule, and no, I dont care, its how we do it, but pattern bleeding takes a point of quintessence if you have it. The damage only comes if you dont. And no, you cant choose damage over quintessence loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 08-21-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T17:35:05-07:00","id":635252,"title":"","content":"Nevermind, didn't make sence and was confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 08-21-2015, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T19:39:29-07:00","id":635330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=635156#post635156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pattern bleeding can be healed with 1 success per day using Life 2. It's insignificant.<br /> I don't think that spheres differences are unfair, it's the house rule that is. Getting paradox for each scene that each buff a mage uses in combat is too much. Mages needs stuff like soaking pools and damage/attack bonus to survive. And the majority of them will let him do things that are pretty incredible for a sleeper to believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to argue whether or not something is fair, as that's an opinion that everyone can decide for themselves. But to say that Mages need stuff like soaking pools and damage bonuses to survive is silly. It is very possible to run an entire Mage chronicle with little or no combat at all. The occasional fight sequence is fun, sure, but it's hardly the be-all and end-all of Mage.<br /> <br /> Some characters are designed for combat, some aren't. One of the jobs of the Storyteller is to suit the chronicle to the characters. If the characters can't manage a pitched battle, then don't force them to do one. Allow them to find alternate solutions and give them alternate challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T20:38:23-07:00","id":635377,"title":"","content":"The description of the Life sphere states that pattern bleeding can be stopped if Prime is used to refill the pattern. Or if the alteration is made permanent, which would require Life 5. <br /> <br /> The part of needing Prime to refill the lost quintessence makes me wonder if it can be healed by Life 2 (which BTW requires 2 successes not 1). Now I'm not saying it can't be healed over time, I'm just wondering if normal Life healing effects are capable of doing so.<br /> <br /> In the past I've always rulled no but then my players rarely have maintained life alteration effects for more than a scene so its never really been an issue that I've had to look up. <br /> <br /> Incedentaly, we've never allowed Life magic alone to heal Avatar damage either though I'm not totally sure pattern damage applies to the Avatar or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T05:21:47-07:00","id":635640,"title":"","content":"First off : It has been mentioned that &quot;nerfing&quot; an effect with a long duration with more paradox would be unfair. I sincerly don't understand this notion. First off : The successes spend on the duration aren't spent to negate paradox in any fashion, that would need prime 5. They are spent for duration, that's it. A char who casts a shield spell with only 2 points spent on duration is set for the day, one who spends 5 or more is set for a long time. The one who spen only 2 may have a stronger shield, but he has to recast it completly the next time he wants to go into a dangerous situation. Especially annoying when the danger finds you suddenly unprepared, which could have been prevented with a longer duration.<br /> <br /> Duration successes are just that, they weren't underpowerd in the dark ages when you wouldn't get paradox and they aren't now. The notion that paradox is associated with the moment of casting the spell is absurd. Sure the rules may make it seem like that, but mostly paradox is about disbleif. So every time your spell does something impossible (vulgar), you get paradox. You are still changing reality, this is an ongoing process, it's just drawn out over a longer time period.<br /> <br /> A hardcore ST who wants to make paradox really hit home may even rule that every soak roll you make with your shield incurs paradox. I personally wouldn't, but it is not a completly crazy idea metaphysically speaking, just depends on the tone you want your setting to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Getting paradox for each scene that each buff a mage uses in combat is too much. Mages needs stuff like soaking pools and damage/attack bonus to survive. </div> </div> </div>They really don't. For once it depends on the kind of char you are playing of course. If you play a char who can't survive without fighting opponents of in vulgar fashion every day (or so) then you are in deep trouble. AS YOU SHOULD BE. I mean come on, that's like a chain smoker saying lung cancer is imbalanced. Though luck, try not to pick so many fights or learn fight them smarter.<br /> <br /> Mages have loads of ways to rig combat in their favour, all completly coincidental. Time 2, Entropy 1 let's you go full out &quot;just as I planned&quot; on everyone trying to ambush you. Mind 2 can easily keep people from attacking you. Entropy 2 can make you hit a perfect headshot with your eyes closed in panic, what are the chances? A combination of Life, Mind and Entropy can enhance your combat skills to truly amazing levels. Sure Werewolf may be fast, but it scant matters if you bring up your sword in just the right moment to go for his brains as he is trying to tackle you. Maybe you can even sidestep it too. Wow those master martial artists surly are scary, he probably trained his whole life to get such good combat instincts. All completly paradox free. Never even an enrgy shield needed. And what if you screw up even though you had those coincidental measures prepared? What if someone breaches them but once? Well nothing is keeping you from having an energy shield as a last ditch defense. Take some paradox, well too bad.<br /> <br /> If you look for a game where mages throw fireballs at each other in dark corners or fight with blows that could shatter mountains then MtA just isn't supposed to be that game. Well actually the latter part may happen from time to time in the hymalajas, the akashic paradigm dominates the concensus there. And there is allways the Umbra for such things. But on earth you don't fight flashy battles against vampires and evil warlocks. Because mage is not a game of physical, but of idiological conflict. You fight for ideas, for public perception. That is what the ascension war is a bout. Technomancers allways developing new stuff to release to the masses, to strengthen their faith that through technology everything is possible. While traditionalists try to keep humanities fading vestiges of belief in the supernatural alife, through various means.<br /> <br /> So yes there are mages that are deiberatly vulgar. Faith healers come to mind (though thanks to large enough sleeper cults they often even slip through the cracks of paradox' attention), activly trying to push the concensus back onto the &quot;right&quot; path. All other mages not so ideologically motivated? They just try to stay coincidental, because otherwise....<br /> <br /> Mage is all about being able to change reality, but finding reality loathe to be pushed around by you. Your potential is unlimited, but the narrowmindedness of the worlds population and (in the case of mystics) the machinations of the TU have made the world itself , the very fabric of reality toxic for you. You can rebel against the status quo and will have to face both reality and those who do not agree with you (what an epic struggle). Or you can choose keep out of the conflict and confine yourself to the limits set by paradox, allways chafing against them. Yes this is irritating as player when playing mage. &quot;I could just fireblast that guy, but then I'd take paradox and I could just have solved this problem without it. Ah fuck, I'll talk him into giving me what I want. &quot; This irritation however is not something bad. It simulates your chars feelings at being kept back when the world could be his to shape as he wants! It also pushes players to really think first because they just do something with magic. Which is good, because magic is not something to be taken lightly. If you do it just for shit and giggles you will be punished by the consequences. Doubly so in MtA.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T06:46:02-07:00","id":635725,"title":"","content":"You may do home rules but please do not call basic game rules absurd. Duration rules always were there in the game.<br /> <br /> Please read your m20 book. It's a pleasant read and we have stuff like rules. I invite you to read page 501. It's basically how you cast spells and how you get punished. There is also a section on paradox. In the life sphere, you have something called pattern bleeding. there are a couple of other nice snippets in the enhancement background. It's 700 pages of goodies. There is even a &quot;table of contents&quot;..<br /> <br /> I started the thread because i wanted to know what the STs would do with absurd situations, like a continuous vulgar effect. While keeping to the rules.<br /> <br /> It's A onyx path forum, i thought we would have kept to the rules and the wod gameworld. I'm sorry to have started this thread now.<br /> <br /> btw, we have our home rules as well, i'm putting up a new thread on our favorite home rules!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","user":"AgentCunningham","date":". 08-22-2015, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T07:27:15-07:00","id":635771,"title":"","content":"Interestingly enough I have very few house rules of which none of the things we've discussed here are included. We are following the rules and where said rules become contradictory and, or hazy we follow what we believe to be the Spirit of the rules. <br /> <br /> One thing im fairly happy with is that in nearly 30 years of GMing RPGs whith a multitude of groups I cant really recal arguments over rules. That doesn't happen if your ignoring, changing or manipulating rules. So you can say what you like, but over the last 15 years of White Wolf games I believe I've followed the rules, and so do my groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:06:50-07:00","id":635813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunningham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=635725#post635725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may do home rules but please do not call basic game rules absurd. Duration rules always were there in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I'm sorry but besides the fact that the rules have been hazy, especially across different editions (and M20 coming out does NOT invalidate anything written previously. Especially stuff that came out to clarify/elaborate on rules that were left vague because in a corebook [like M20, to a degree, is] wasn't enough space for it.), and at times even contradictory inside one book, part of the topic (unblief) has been left (I wager deliberatly) vague in description. So there is no hard and fast rule. If you choose to just set everything not specifically numbered in the books aside as nonexistent then yeah there is no unblief and paradox is only incurred very infrequently. In fact I'd encourage you to do away with paradox completly in this case since it will become a meaningless mechanic that barely does anything, instead just let magic botches play out more harshly. Of course such a world needs certain &quot;maneuvering&quot; by the ST to stay in any shape comparable to our own.<br /> <br /> And aside from all of this : Yes I will call basic game rules absurd if they do not reflect the flavour of the oWoD. oWoD has allways been a game based around elaborate fluff instead of solid crunch. In basically all worlds rules have been left vague in parts to encourage STs to adjust the setting slightly without straying too far from an established world. What you describe is not the &quot;right&quot; way of doing things. It is merly one way of doing things, all keeping to the core rules for the most part. You asked us how we as an ST would deal with this kind of situation. Given the prominent station of the golden rule in the oWoD line you will find awnsers that differ from on another. You just have to keep an open mind here and not try to find a law written in the holy book of M20. Most argued from a point that considered the established setting and it's metaphysics, rather than a page quotation.<br /> <br /> I do have homerules. Shifted around some spherelevels etc. and I'm happy to discuss those, but this paradox issue ist really just discussion your perception of the grey areas left by the book. Well that and paradox regarding effects with a duration. You may call it a homerule if you want, but really anything else makes no sense given the setting. The (magely) supernatural would never have stayed hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:42:17-07:00","id":635835,"title":"","content":"Hazy? Please donot call the basic rules absurd or hazy! There are tons of rules that we can argue about, but rules that are in the magical summary sheet that is the cornerstone of the game cannot be hazy or absurd.<br /> <br /> It's ok not to be in accordance with them and modify them to your gaming geoup content. <br /> <br /> In my book, A vulgar effect should generate more than 1 paradox point like in the revised book, but i understand why it was changed in the m20 book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","user":"AgentCunningham","date":".  Too insulting, modified it 08-22-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:51:15-07:00","id":635851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunningham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=635725#post635725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may do home rules but please do not call basic game rules absurd. Duration rules always were there in the game.<br /> <br /> Please read your m20 book. It's a pleasant read and we have stuff like rules. I invite you to read page 501. It's basically how you cast spells and how you get punished. There is also a section on paradox. In the life sphere, you have something called pattern bleeding. there are a couple of other nice snippets in the enhancement background. It's 700 pages of goodies. There is even a &quot;table of contents&quot;..<br /> <br /> I started the thread because i wanted to know what the STs would do with absurd situations, like a continuous vulgar effect. While keeping to the rules.<br /> <br /> It's A onyx path forum, i thought we would have kept to the rules and the wod gameworld. I'm sorry to have started this thread now.<br /> <br /> btw, we have our home rules as well, i'm putting up a new thread on our favorite home rules!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting position, because you have repeatedly ignored other people citing rule examples that contradict yours in both this thread and the Life Rituals thread. (Including the citation on Permadox from Mage 20)<br /> <br /> In the end, it seems like you're only interested in reciting your particular interpretation of the rules, a lot of which would also constitute House Rules (If it isn't explicitly stated in M20, and it isn't in a previous edition either, then it's a House Rule. See: your Sanctum interpretation from the Life Rituals text.) So your position in this post is just a little hypocritical.<br /> <br /> The happy fact of Mage is that rules are often contradictory and incomplete at best. Mage 20, in particular, has shortened specific sections (specifically Spheres and Paradox) in anticipation of future books. (I want the promised Sphere book so badly I can taste it.) Everyone accepts these shortcomings, even the creators, and house rules are expressly encouraged in the text. In this thread, the question was how we would deal with 'reassert reality' which led to a discussion on the handling of paradox. You've received a lot of answers which did not suit your game style. That doesn't make you right and us wrong, or vice versa. You asked. We answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 08-22-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T09:04:16-07:00","id":635882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunningham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=635835#post635835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hazy? Please donot call the basic rules absurd or hazy! There are tons of rules that we can argue about, but rules that are in the magical summary sheet that is the cornerstone of the game cannot be hazy or absurd.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is kind of the same thing awnsered to last time. There is plenty of haze in the rules. More specifically just because something isn't touched upon in the summary sheet does not mean it does not exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my book, A vulgar effect should generate more than 1 paradox point like in the revised book, but i understand why it was changed in the m20 book. </div> </div> </div>This is a good example. While M20 goes with 1 point of paradox as default, it also has a sidebar following immediatly after saying &quot;Hey if the Avatar Storm/something similar happened in your game or is even still going on maybe you want to use these harsher rules&quot;. M20th especially has a lot of sidebars basically screaming &quot;There were different rules over the editions, just choose whatever you like.&quot; This is why M20 is a bad place to look for hard and fast rules. And this is a good thing!<br /> <br /> Personally I btw. give out 1 paradox if there was no witness around and use the revised paradox for vulgar with witness. Which would be a good example of a houserule.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T09:09:01-07:00","id":635884,"title":"","content":"Err i have never contradicted myself, you must be writing of somebody else. <br /> <br /> You make a magick spell. Is it coincidental or vulgar? If vulgar you get a point of paradox.<br /> Exception is life magic (pattern bleeding, enhancement,genetic flaws). <br /> If at the point of casting you affect the outside of yoursanctum, it can be vulgar.<br /> <br /> As for being answered, i got a lot of opinions and home rules. Thank you for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T09:24:11-07:00","id":635920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunningham</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=635835#post635835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hazy? Please donot call the basic rules absurd or hazy! There are tons of rules that we can argue about, but rules that are in the magical summary sheet that is the cornerstone of the game cannot be hazy or absurd.<br /> <br /> It's ok not to be in accordance with them and modify them to your gaming geoup content.<br /> <br /> In my book, A vulgar effect should generate more than 1 paradox point like in the revised book, but i understand why it was changed in the m20 book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dear. That's a silly statement. Of course game rules can be hazy and absurd. Real world laws are hazy and absurd sometimes and they actually matter. The problem is that rules are written by humans, and we're all a bit flawed sometimes.<br /> <br /> One of the things that made World of Darkness special to me when I played originally, and now, was that unlike some other games, there was an open acknowledgement at the beginning of each book that the rules weren't going to cover every eventuality or suit every playstyle. That the creators of the games expected players to modify, replace and discard rules at will. That was an amazing idea to me, and really emphasized to me that these are games that are, first and foremost, about everyone having fun.<br /> <br /> They gave us the Golden Rule, which is reprinted in every core rulebook, and I suspect every supplemental book as well, which supersedes every other rule in the games (including all of the helpful charts): &quot;<i>The rules are what you want them to be.</i>&quot; (Page 384 in M20.) I'd recommend checking out page 22 and 23 for help with the sandbox nature of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 08-22-2015, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:22:50-07:00","id":636092,"title":"","content":"I'm with AgentCunningham on this. The official M20 rules states that paradox is gained on the moment of casting and it's pretty simple. Coincident: No paradox. Vulgar: 1 paradox. Botch have revised rules. That's it. So, anything that doesn't follow this rule is a house rule, and this isn't a bad thing. Just isn't the official. All the sidebars on M20 are house rules.<br /> <br /> Flinty, excelent post taht you replied to me. You are right about the unfairness, but I still think that permadox gets a lot of space with this house rule. I'd rather get 1 permadox soaking everything with Life 3 instead of getting a lot of paradox (every time that the mage soaks, which deppending on the ST could be a lot) with other kind of defenses. You could argue that Life is a more powerful sphere for those who want to be a fighting machine.Ok ,maybe this is right.<br /> <br /> If you want your rules to make sense with the Mage scenario, then you should get paradox everytime that any effect or it's consequences aren't believable. This martial artist could'nt fight 4+ guys in the same time, no matter how lucky he is, he would be getting paradox for every punch that he blocks.<br /> A rule like this would ruin the game, and the one you use (1 dox for the scene) just don't makes more sense than the official 1 for effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:24:54-07:00","id":636095,"title":"","content":"No, sidebars are not &quot;house rules&quot;, they are &quot;optional rules&quot;. House rules are something that an individual storyteller creates (or adapts) to suit their individual purposes. Optional rules have been published by official sources and are just that: optional. You're really going to need to keep these terms straight, if you're going to manage the game. Particularly if/when you seek information/advice from the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T12:50:28-07:00","id":636200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=636092#post636092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think that permadox gets a lot of space with this house rule. I'd rather get 1 permadox soaking everything with Life 3 instead of getting a lot of paradox (every time that the mage soaks, which deppending on the ST could be a lot) with other kind of defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the permanent shield could also result in permadox instead of paradox each time really. Or the Life effect could result in paradox each time instead of permadox. And yes this would a be houserule. As a ST I kinda would choose one of those and then keep to it for spells that have a long situation and are potentially vulgar. Handling it different for different spheres doesn't make too much sense for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want your rules to make sense with the Mage scenario, then you should get paradox everytime that any effect or it's consequences aren't believable. </div> </div> </div>And why would I want anything else? That said, if I threw 3 firebally in quick sucession as the result of one channeled spell over three rounds or three spells in a single roll each turn, why would I get more paradox for one? It is kind of hard to find a hard and fast rule to quantify this (and it is certainly homebrew), but the amount of paradox should diminish with each like vulgar effect cast. Especially if witnesses are there (afterall cleary that guy CAN throw fireballs). I also think it would be conceivable for mages to &quot;copy&quot; static magic they just witnessed and thus slip through paradox' notice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This martial artist could'nt fight 4+ guys in the same time, no matter how lucky he is, he would be getting paradox for every punch that he blocks. </div> </div> </div>I think you mistake something here. Coincidental spells are not bound to what is realistically possible, but what is arguably believable. Would a martial artist win against 5 opponents (with a bit of training and teamwork) at once? Probably not often. But maybe 1 out of 10 times. You magic ensures it is going to be that one time. Sure do it often enough and the domino effect will hound you a bit, but that's about it. Furthermore it's also about what the average joe would think possible. Sure a normal guys couldn't take on 5 people at once, but with some kung fu willy nilly, who knows? Movies like the Batman franchise may be contrived, but the average Joe would say it's at least possible (well the tech may be a few years ahead but who knows what the goverments been hiding form us!). You just happen to be extremly lucky.<br /> <br /> This is also the point where defining vulgar becomes hard. Enemies gun just happens to jam? Well shit happens. All the guns in the whole hit squad are jammed??? Might be vulgar, but maybe you could have sabotaged them, actually kind of depends on the situation and how well the hit squad took care of their weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A rule like this would ruin the game, and the one you use (1 dox for the scene) just don't makes more sense than the official 1 for effect. </div> </div> </div>See a bit above. It is just very hard to find a functioning rule for it, so yes 'dox per scene is far from perfect, but it's far better than none. And actually still a rule like this wouldn't ruin the game, you'd just have to be extra careful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T21:04:32-07:00","id":636628,"title":"","content":"Wow, this thread grew fast...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of my post its that, because of several &quot;holes&quot; in the rules, all of these things won't happen (or would be irrelevant). Even giving Paradox when the magic it's &quot;activated&quot; seems to be outside of the rules for our OP. So no, no Paradox realm (nor a single Paradox point) for the lucky dragon summoner that knows so well the rules of Mage. That's the point.<br /> Is that the setting you saw when you readed the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how a Paradox Backlash can be even more outlandish than the spell that birthed it?<br /> <br /> Yes, it is indeed.<br /> <br /> I said what I would do independently of the book, but even then, seriously, what holds the setting is itself.<br /> <br /> The TU don't need to make everyone forget it. Though they could try, and the only thing to stop them from succeeding would be Tradition Mages. What they need to do is to make key people forget and control media. Other people will take care of themselves. One person sees the dragons, looks around the day after, sees that a lot of other people didn't remember anything wrong. She will either assume it as a nightmare or become insane. Either way, it works.<br /> <br /> Just look a little on the internet and see how much people believe in crazy stuff, sometimes about things everyone else saw. See the conspiracy theories, the UFOs, ghost sightings on crowded streets. Turn that up for the World of Darkness, because Real Life isn't all that serious either. And if something really huge happens, they can just use a few Procedures and turn one thing into another. What about 9/11? WTC was brought down by airplanes? In the Mage setting it could very well be the 10 dragons. A lot of people died, a lot of destruction ensued, the TU can't cover everything. But they don't need to. Just turn it into something else, use a Procedure to find people that made records and change <u>their</u> minds and records. Most witnesses are quite traumatized anyway. IRL you can play a lot with people memories if you control their ways to reassure those memories. Imagine in WoD?<br /> <br /> By the way, neither spirits nor other creatures need Paradox rules to exist. They can come after the Mage out of simple necessity (to stop her) or vengeance. Judicious use of Time and Entropy magic, or simply Auspex Discipline or some spiritual advice can alert freaking every single supernatural society in miles that a crazy summoner is trying to bring 10 dragons. There are ways to alert the entire supernatural world that the stupidest ritual in recent history will take place.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Elder Disciplines can be incredible vulgar without ever accruing Paradox. If you thing this is a problem in Mage, you'll never accept the Masquerade exists. As <b>Ambrosia</b> said: Week of Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize that many times people consider a game that needs house rules or the Golden Rule of GMing to work must be broken or is being ran by an incompetent GM. It should be remembered though that the game rules aren't written by lawyers. If they were then most loopholes and contradictions wouldn't be there to be exploited. The book would probably be 3 times as big though and we would all need law degrees to understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, but the rules of the game ARE broken, and there are a huge RPG market out there to prove that better rules are possible without the need of a lawyer. You have a good grasp of what is needed to play cWoD, but those need are precisely because the rules ARE badly written.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentCunninghan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please donot call the basic rules absurd or hazy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hazy. They are, always where, and at M20 still being. When I get tired of hazy rules, I go for nWoD. It seems that Awakening 2nd edition will have some pretty solid rules. 1st edition is already far more clear than Ascension. But then, Ascension does have a lot of amazing things in the setting. The drawback? Incredibly hazy rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 08-23-2015, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T04:24:27-07:00","id":636879,"title":"","content":"Basic casting reference chart, page 500-510. 1 vulgar effect= 1 botch. Only exception is life magic in it's description. It's pretty easy and clear cut. <br /> <br /> The writers wrote a wonderful new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7358-agentcunningham","name":"AgentCunningham","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T09:36:59-07:00","id":637105,"title":"","content":"The chart does not take into account every eventuality, and occasionally contradicts other parts of the text. One example is Wonders. By way the chart reads, a Wonder should only incur Paradox on creation. However, the Wonders and Paradox section later in the book expressly contradicts this, and addresses circumstances where use of the Wonder can cause Paradox. There is nothing in the book that says, &quot;in case of contradiction, the chart wins out.&quot; The fact of the matter is that an individual storyteller must decide which rule is appropriate for her game. <br /> <br /> (Another example of something the chart doesn't address is p. 533's Unbelief. It is clear from reading that section that Unbelief will still be in effect after initial creation. There isn't a precise rule in that section, however, so that's something a storyteller needs to decide. Basically, if the charts covered everything needed to run the Mage game, M20 would be 40 pages rather than 600+)<br /> <br /> Mage 20's section on magick (specifically spheres and Paradox) is much smaller than most of the other editions' sections. This isn't a bad thing as they still give us enough to go on. However, there will be a Guide to the Spheres posted soon. That book may resolve a lot of lingering questions/contradictions. Though, in the grand tradition of Mage the Ascension, I'm sure it will introduce even more contradictions and loopholes.<br /> <br /> Mage 20 is a wonderful, magnificent edition of Mage the Ascension, but like every edition of Mage the Ascension, it has its flaws and loopholes. And storytellers will find their own way to deal with them. If you ask the forum a hypothetical involving a potential loophole, as in this thread, you should not be surprised that experienced Storytellers already have their own ways of plugging the loophole (or, per their reading of the rules, don't see the loophole as existing at all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T17:52:20-07:00","id":638542,"title":"","content":"If you are seeing clear rules in Ascension, there's something <u>very</u> wrong with your eyes, seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T03:55:42-07:00","id":640039,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time not liking that post, AND chuckling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-30T20:12:19-07:00","id":1446723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=634567#post634567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A giant energy ball always generate normal Paradox, which means that I don't have to houserule anything in this case. In this case the rules work as intended (it's a Vulgar display).<br /> But that's besides the point.<br /> <br /> As I said,<b> the problem it's not the mage, but to keep those &quot;in game situations&quot; that you speak about from destroying the setting.</b><br /> I don't care if the mage get's punished or escapes and lives happily thereafter. Of course such actions will demand reprimand from in game factions. What I do care it's that such actions may call for an unrealistic response or blow the setting.<br /> <br /> Either humanity discover that magic it's real, or an Archmage steps in and reverses time, or Technocracy brainwashes everyone. As Tuch says, there're plenty of ways of wrecking the game, and plenty of ways of impeding these.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you're so hung up on this. If you are a member of the traditions, shouldn't this be your ultimate goal? To destroy the consensus and prove that magic exists. You want to make such a big mess that the Technocracy can't just brainwash the event away.<br /> <br /> EDIT: If you're able to summon dragons to attack Manhattan, you have enough spheres that you're in the endgame phase of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T11:33:30-07:00","id":1446815,"title":"","content":"I see your proficiency in the necromantic arts it's impressive, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2078_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2078\" data-vbnamecard=\"2078\">Alucard</a><br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't think I would be so adamant about that nowdays<br /> <br /> I still think the old rule it's better for a plethora of reasons - It really makes sense, for many situations<br /> <br /> Think that this is how normaly magick interacts with the world: The Vulgarity of the spell depends on the place it's going to be used (For instance: It's not the same casting inside the Umbra than casting <i>from </i>the Umbra <i>to</i> Earth ).<br /> <br /> The Sanctum example seems to me like a &quot;gotcha&quot; situation. It takes advantage on a loophole, that could happen in a lot of scenarios because Paradox it's determined at the moment of casting, and the ST isn't omniscient (It could happen even w/o intent from the players. Like, the Sanctum walls collapse just after the casting of an extremely Vulgar, lasting, thing). I don't think it's the spirit of the rules to allow this<br /> <br /> BUT. I grant that<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9KGfgg-d8s&amp;ab_channel=BobbyK\" target=\"_blank\"> I exaggerated a little </a> :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-01-2021, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:46:17-07:00","id":1446885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/633531-reasserting-reality?p=1446815#post1446815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your proficiency in the necromantic arts it's impressive, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2078_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2078\" data-vbnamecard=\"2078\">Alucard</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry about that. <br /> <br /> I do a lot of deep dives on topics and read all the threads about them. The problem is that I leave a lot of tabs open. Then I come back to it a day or two later and continue reading, while forgetting that the thread is really old. Then I see something I want to reply to and this happens.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}